import TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Charpoly.FinTwo

/-!
# Four-twist weights of orbit tori and the signed iterates of the return map

Let `φ` be an area-preserving diffeomorphism of a closed surface and `Y_φ` its mapping torus. In
the symplectic four-manifold `S¹ × Y_φ` a periodic orbit `γ` of `φ` gives an embedded
square-zero torus `S¹ × γ`, and the normal operator of this torus is governed by the linearized
return map `P` of `γ`, a `2 × 2` matrix of determinant one. Of the four normal operators of the
torus twisted by its real sign characters, the two twisted along the circle factor are expected to
have positive determinant sign, while the untwisted operator and the operator twisted only along
`γ` compare with `det (1 - P)` and `det (1 + P)`. The four-twist label `(σ, i)` of Taubes's
weighted count that these signs prescribe has `σ` the sign of `det (1 - P)`, and `i` equal to `1`
or `0` according as `det (1 + P)` is negative or not. Since `det (1 ∓ P) = 2 ∓ trace P`, a
return map all of whose iterates are nondegenerate falls into one of three classes:

* positive hyperbolic (`2 < trace P`), with label `(-, 0)` and local series `1 - t`;
* negative hyperbolic (`trace P < -2`), with label `(+, 1)` and local series `1 + t`;
* elliptic (`|trace P| < 2`), with label `(+, 0)` and local series `1 / (1 - t)`.

This file proves that in each class the local series `f = f_(σ, i)` of `TauCeti.torusWeightSeries`
satisfies the logarithmic derivative identity

`t f'(t) = f(t) ∑_{k ≥ 1} ε(P ^ k) t ^ k`,    `ε(Q) = sgn det (1 - Q)`,

provided every iterate of `P` is nondegenerate, `det (1 - P ^ k) ≠ 0` for `k ≥ 1`. Here `ε(P ^ k)`
is the Lefschetz index of the fixed point of the `k`-th iterate of the return map. Over `ℚ` the
identity says that `log f = ∑_{k ≥ 1} ε(P ^ k) t ^ k / k`, so that `f` is the factor that the orbit
`γ` contributes to the dynamical zeta function `exp ∑_n L(φ ^ n) t ^ n / n`. Taubes's weights of
the orbit tori thus reproduce the local factors of the Lefschetz zeta function, which is the local
input to the comparison of the curve count of `S¹ × Y_φ` with the zeta function of `φ`.

That the determinant signs of the twisted normal operators of the orbit torus are those of
`det (1 ∓ P)` is a determinant comparison which this file does not prove; the statements here are
about the label that the signs of `det (1 ∓ P)` prescribe.

The label is the one that `TauCeti.twistIndex` attaches to sign data on the sign characters of the
torus. Write `H₁(S¹ × γ; ℤ) = ℤ × ℤ`, the first factor generated by the circle `S¹` and the second
by the orbit `γ`. The signs prescribed by the return map (`TauCeti.orbitTorusTwistSign`) are `+`
on the two sign characters that are nontrivial on `S¹`, `sgn det (1 - P)` on the trivial
character and `sgn det (1 + P)` on the character that is nontrivial on `γ` only. Their twist index
is `1` or `0` according as `det (1 + P)` is negative or not
(`TauCeti.twistIndex_orbitTorusTwistSign`). The orbit traversed twice has return map `P ^ 2`, and
its orbit torus is the double cover of `S¹ × γ` defined by the character nontrivial on `γ` only
(that is, trivial on `S¹`). Its
untwisted sign is the product of the two signs of `S¹ × γ` trivial on `S¹`, since
`1 - P ^ 2 = (1 - P) (1 + P)` (`TauCeti.orbitTorusTwistSign_sq_zero`), and its twist index is
`0`, since `det (1 + P ^ 2) = (trace P) ^ 2` is never negative when `det P = 1`
(`TauCeti.twistIndex_orbitTorusTwistSign_sq`).

## Main results

* `TauCeti.mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_forall_pos`,
  `TauCeti.mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_forall_neg`,
  `TauCeti.mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_trace_lt_neg_two`: the series
  `∑_{k ≥ 1} sgn det (1 - P ^ k) t ^ k` is `t / (1 - t)` when every `det (1 - P ^ k)` is positive,
  `-t / (1 - t)` when every `det (1 - P ^ k)` is negative, and `t / (1 + t)` for a negative
  hyperbolic return map.
* `TauCeti.X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_false_zero_of_two_lt_trace`: the identity for a
  positive hyperbolic return map and the series `f_(-, 0) = 1 - t`.
* `TauCeti.X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_true_one_of_trace_lt_neg_two`: the identity for a
  negative hyperbolic return map and the series `f_(+, 1) = 1 + t`.
* `TauCeti.X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_true_zero_of_abs_trace_le_two`: the identity for a
  nondegenerate elliptic return map and the series `f_(+, 0) = 1 / (1 - t)`.
* `TauCeti.X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_of_det_eq_one`: the identity for every return map
  all of whose iterates are nondegenerate, with the label read off from the signs of
  `det (1 - P)` and `det (1 + P)`.
* `TauCeti.X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_orbitTorusTwistSign`: the same identity, with the
  label `(σ, i)` computed by `TauCeti.twistLabel` from the signs `TauCeti.orbitTorusTwistSign`
  on the sign characters of the orbit torus.

## References

* C. H. Taubes, *Counting pseudo-holomorphic submanifolds in dimension 4*,
  J. Differential Geom. 44 (1996), 818--893.
* E.-N. Ionel and T. H. Parker, *Gromov invariants and symplectic maps*, Math. Ann. 314 (1999),
  127--158.
* M. Hutchings and Y.-J. Lee, *Circle-valued Morse theory, Reidemeister torsion, and
  Seiberg–Witten invariants of 3-manifolds*, Topology 38 (1999), 861--888.
-/

public section

open PowerSeries Matrix

namespace TauCeti

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [LinearOrder R] [IsStrictOrderedRing R]
  {P : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R}

omit [IsStrictOrderedRing R] in
/-- If every iterate `P ^ k`, `k ≥ 1`, has `0 < det (1 - P ^ k)`, then the signs
`sgn det (1 - P ^ k)`, `k ≥ 1`, sum to `∑_{k ≥ 1} t ^ k = t / (1 - t)`. -/
theorem mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_forall_pos (hP : ∀ k ≠ 0, 0 < (1 - P ^ k).det) :
    (mk fun k ↦ if k = 0 then 0 else (SignType.sign (1 - P ^ k).det : ℤ)) = X * mk 1 := by
  ext (_ | k)
  · simp
  · simp [sign_pos (hP _ k.succ_ne_zero), coeff_succ_X_mul]

omit [IsStrictOrderedRing R] in
/-- If every iterate `P ^ k`, `k ≥ 1`, has `det (1 - P ^ k) < 0`, then the signs
`sgn det (1 - P ^ k)`, `k ≥ 1`, sum to `-∑_{k ≥ 1} t ^ k = -t / (1 - t)`. -/
theorem mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_forall_neg (hP : ∀ k ≠ 0, (1 - P ^ k).det < 0) :
    (mk fun k ↦ if k = 0 then 0 else (SignType.sign (1 - P ^ k).det : ℤ)) = -(X * mk 1) := by
  ext (_ | k)
  · simp
  · simp [sign_neg (hP _ k.succ_ne_zero), coeff_succ_X_mul]

/-- For a negative hyperbolic `2 × 2` matrix `P` of determinant one (`trace P < -2`), the signs
`sgn det (1 - P ^ k) = (-1) ^ (k + 1)`, `k ≥ 1`, sum to
`∑_{k ≥ 1} (-1) ^ (k + 1) t ^ k = t / (1 + t)`. -/
theorem mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_trace_lt_neg_two (hdet : P.det = 1) (htr : P.trace < -2) :
    (mk fun k ↦ if k = 0 then 0 else (SignType.sign (1 - P ^ k).det : ℤ)) =
      X * mk fun k ↦ (-1) ^ k := by
  ext (_ | k)
  · simp
  · rw [coeff_mk, ite_eq_right k.succ_ne_zero,
      sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_trace_lt_neg_two hdet htr k.succ_ne_zero, coeff_succ_X_mul, coeff_mk,
      pow_succ, pow_succ]
    ring

/-- For a positive hyperbolic `2 × 2` matrix `P` of determinant one (`2 < trace P`), the local
series `f_(-, 0) = 1 - t` satisfies `t f' = f ∑_{k ≥ 1} sgn det (1 - P ^ k) t ^ k`: every iterate
of `P` has `det (1 - P ^ k) < 0`, and `1 - t = exp (-∑_{k ≥ 1} t ^ k / k)`. -/
theorem X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_false_zero_of_two_lt_trace (hdet : P.det = 1)
    (htr : 2 < P.trace) :
    X * d⁄dX (torusWeightSeries false 0) = torusWeightSeries false 0 *
      mk fun k ↦ if k = 0 then 0 else (SignType.sign (1 - P ^ k).det : ℤ) := by
  -- Both sides are `-X`, as `(1 - X) * mk 1 = 1`.
  rw [mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_forall_neg fun k hk ↦
      det_one_sub_pow_neg_of_two_lt_trace hdet htr hk, torusWeightSeries_false_zero]
  simp only [map_sub, derivative_one, derivative_X]
  linear_combination X * mk_one_mul_one_sub_eq_one (S := ℤ)

/-- For a negative hyperbolic `2 × 2` matrix `P` of determinant one (`trace P < -2`), the local
series `f_(+, 1) = 1 + t` satisfies `t f' = f ∑_{k ≥ 1} sgn det (1 - P ^ k) t ^ k`: the sign of
`det (1 - P ^ k)` is `(-1) ^ (k + 1)`, and `1 + t = exp ∑_{k ≥ 1} (-1) ^ (k + 1) t ^ k / k`. -/
theorem X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_true_one_of_trace_lt_neg_two (hdet : P.det = 1)
    (htr : P.trace < -2) :
    X * d⁄dX (torusWeightSeries true 1) = torusWeightSeries true 1 *
      mk fun k ↦ if k = 0 then 0 else (SignType.sign (1 - P ^ k).det : ℤ) := by
  -- Both sides are `X`, as `(mk fun k ↦ (-1) ^ k) * (1 + X) = 1`.
  rw [mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_trace_lt_neg_two hdet htr, torusWeightSeries_true_one]
  simp only [map_add, derivative_one, derivative_X]
  linear_combination (-X) * mk_neg_one_pow_mul_one_add_eq_one (S := ℤ)

/-- For a `2 × 2` matrix `P` of determinant one with `|trace P| ≤ 2`, all of whose iterates are
nondegenerate (so that `P` is elliptic), the local series `f_(+, 0) = 1 / (1 - t)` satisfies
`t f' = f ∑_{k ≥ 1} sgn det (1 - P ^ k) t ^ k`: every iterate has `0 < det (1 - P ^ k)`, and
`1 / (1 - t) = exp ∑_{k ≥ 1} t ^ k / k`. -/
theorem X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_true_zero_of_abs_trace_le_two (hdet : P.det = 1)
    (htr : |P.trace| ≤ 2) (hP : ∀ k ≠ 0, (1 - P ^ k).det ≠ 0) :
    X * d⁄dX (torusWeightSeries true 0) = torusWeightSeries true 0 *
      mk fun k ↦ if k = 0 then 0 else (SignType.sign (1 - P ^ k).det : ℤ) := by
  -- Both sides are `∑ k X ^ k`, the right side being `X * (mk 1) ^ 2`.
  rw [mk_sign_det_one_sub_pow_of_forall_pos fun k hk ↦
      (det_one_sub_pow_nonneg_of_abs_trace_le_two hdet htr k).lt_of_ne' (hP k hk),
    torusWeightSeries_true_zero, mul_left_comm, ← sq]
  ext (_ | n)
  · simp
  · rw [coeff_succ_X_mul, coeff_succ_X_mul, coeff_derivative, mk_one_pow_eq_mk_choose_add]
    simp [add_comm]

/-- **Orbit-torus weights are local zeta factors.** Let `P` be a `2 × 2` matrix of determinant
one all of whose iterates are nondegenerate, `det (1 - P ^ k) ≠ 0` for `k ≥ 1`. Read off the label
`σ = (0 < det (1 - P))` and `i = 1` if `det (1 + P) < 0`, `i = 0` otherwise. Then the local series
`f = f_(σ, i)` satisfies `t f' = f ∑_{k ≥ 1} sgn det (1 - P ^ k) t ^ k`; over `ℚ` this says
`log f = ∑_{k ≥ 1} sgn det (1 - P ^ k) t ^ k / k`. -/
theorem X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_of_det_eq_one (hdet : P.det = 1)
    (hP : ∀ k ≠ 0, (1 - P ^ k).det ≠ 0) :
    X * d⁄dX (torusWeightSeries (decide (0 < (1 - P).det)) (if (1 + P).det < 0 then 1 else 0)) =
      torusWeightSeries (decide (0 < (1 - P).det)) (if (1 + P).det < 0 then 1 else 0) *
        mk fun k ↦ if k = 0 then 0 else (SignType.sign (1 - P ^ k).det : ℤ) := by
  have h₁ : (1 - P).det = 2 - P.trace := by
    rw [Matrix.det_one_sub_fin_two, hdet]
    ring
  have h₂ : (1 + P).det = 2 + P.trace := by
    rw [Matrix.det_one_add_fin_two, hdet]
    ring
  rw [h₁, h₂]
  rcases lt_or_ge 2 P.trace with htr | htr
  · rw [decide_eq_false (by linarith), ite_eq_right (by linarith)]
    exact X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_false_zero_of_two_lt_trace hdet htr
  rcases lt_or_ge P.trace (-2) with htr' | htr'
  · rw [decide_eq_true (by linarith), ite_eq_left (by linarith)]
    exact X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_true_one_of_trace_lt_neg_two hdet htr'
  have hne : 2 - P.trace ≠ 0 := by simpa [h₁] using hP 1 one_ne_zero
  rw [decide_eq_true (lt_of_le_of_ne (by linarith) hne.symm), ite_eq_right (by linarith)]
  exact X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_true_zero_of_abs_trace_le_two hdet
    (abs_le.2 ⟨htr', htr⟩) hP

/-! ### The label from the sign characters of the orbit torus -/

/-- The determinant signs that the return map `P` prescribes for the normal operators of an orbit
torus `S¹ × γ` twisted by its sign characters `χ : ℤ × ℤ → ℤ/2`, where `H₁(S¹ × γ; ℤ) = ℤ × ℤ`
with the first factor generated by the circle `S¹` and the second by the orbit `γ`. The sign is
`+` when `χ` is nontrivial on `S¹`; otherwise it is `sgn det (1 - P)` or `sgn det (1 + P)`
according as `χ` is trivial on `γ` or not. -/
noncomputable def orbitTorusTwistSign (P : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R) (χ : ℤ × ℤ →+ ZMod 2) :
    SignType :=
  if χ (1, 0) = 0 then
    if χ (0, 1) = 0 then SignType.sign (1 - P).det else SignType.sign (1 + P).det
  else 1

omit [IsStrictOrderedRing R] in
theorem orbitTorusTwistSign_def (P : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R) (χ : ℤ × ℤ →+ ZMod 2) :
    orbitTorusTwistSign P χ = if χ (1, 0) = 0 then
      if χ (0, 1) = 0 then SignType.sign (1 - P).det else SignType.sign (1 + P).det
    else 1 := (rfl)

omit [IsStrictOrderedRing R] in
/-- The untwisted sign of an orbit torus is the sign of `det (1 - P)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem orbitTorusTwistSign_zero (P : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R) :
    orbitTorusTwistSign P 0 = SignType.sign (1 - P).det := by
  simp [orbitTorusTwistSign_def]

omit [IsStrictOrderedRing R] in
/-- The twist index of an orbit torus is `1` if `det (1 + P) < 0` and `0` otherwise: of the three
nontrivial sign characters, only the one trivial on the circle can carry a negative sign. -/
theorem twistIndex_orbitTorusTwistSign (P : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R) :
    twistIndex (orbitTorusTwistSign P) = if (1 + P).det < 0 then 1 else 0 := by
  let ι : ℤ × ℤ →+ ZMod 2 := (Int.castAddHom (ZMod 2)).comp (AddMonoidHom.snd ℤ ℤ)
  let χ : ℤ × ℤ →+ ZMod 2 := (Int.castAddHom (ZMod 2)).comp (AddMonoidHom.fst ℤ ℤ)
  have hι : ι ≠ 0 := fun h ↦ by simpa [ι] using DFunLike.congr_fun h (0, 1)
  have hχ₀ : χ ≠ 0 := fun h ↦ by simpa [χ] using DFunLike.congr_fun h (1, 0)
  have hχι : χ ≠ ι := fun h ↦ by simpa [χ, ι] using DFunLike.congr_fun h (1, 0)
  have hrank : Module.finrank ℤ (ℤ × ℤ) = 2 := by simp
  rw [twistIndex_eq_of_finrank_eq_two hrank hι hχ₀ hχι]
  simp [orbitTorusTwistSign_def, ι, χ, sign_eq_neg_one_iff]

/-- The untwisted sign of the orbit torus of the doubled orbit, with return map `P ^ 2`, is the
product of the signs of `det (1 - P)` and `det (1 + P)`: the signs of the two sign characters of
`S¹ × γ` that are trivial on the double cover defined by the character nontrivial on `γ` only. -/
theorem orbitTorusTwistSign_sq_zero (P : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R) :
    orbitTorusTwistSign (P ^ 2) 0 = orbitTorusTwistSign P 0 * SignType.sign (1 + P).det := by
  rw [orbitTorusTwistSign_zero, orbitTorusTwistSign_zero, ← sign_mul, ← det_mul]
  congr 2
  noncomm_ring

/-- For `det P = 1`, the orbit torus of the doubled orbit has twist index `0`, since
`det (1 + P ^ 2) = (trace P) ^ 2` is never negative. -/
theorem twistIndex_orbitTorusTwistSign_sq (hdet : P.det = 1) :
    twistIndex (orbitTorusTwistSign (P ^ 2)) = 0 := by
  have h : (1 + P ^ 2).det = P.trace ^ 2 := by
    rw [det_one_add_fin_two, det_pow, Matrix.sq_eq_trace_smul_sub_det_smul_one_fin_two P, hdet]
    simp only [one_smul, trace_sub, trace_smul, smul_eq_mul, trace_one, Fintype.card_fin,
      Nat.cast_ofNat, one_pow]
    ring
  rw [twistIndex_orbitTorusTwistSign, h]
  exact ite_eq_right (not_lt.2 (sq_nonneg _))

omit [IsStrictOrderedRing R] in
/-- The twist label of an orbit torus is `1` if `det (1 + P) < 0` and `0` otherwise. -/
theorem twistLabel_orbitTorusTwistSign (P : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) R) :
    twistLabel (by simp) (orbitTorusTwistSign P) = if (1 + P).det < 0 then 1 else 0 := by
  refine Fin.ext ?_
  rw [val_twistLabel, twistIndex_orbitTorusTwistSign]
  split_ifs <;> simp

/-- **Orbit-torus weights are local zeta factors, with the label from the sign characters.** For a
`2 × 2` matrix `P` of determinant one all of whose iterates are nondegenerate, the local series
`f = f_(σ, i)` with `σ = (s 0 = +)` and `i` the twist label of the signs
`s = TauCeti.orbitTorusTwistSign P` satisfies `t f' = f ∑_{k ≥ 1} sgn det (1 - P ^ k) t ^ k`. -/
theorem X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_orbitTorusTwistSign (hdet : P.det = 1)
    (hP : ∀ k ≠ 0, (1 - P ^ k).det ≠ 0) :
    X * d⁄dX (torusWeightSeries (decide (orbitTorusTwistSign P 0 = 1))
        (twistLabel (by simp) (orbitTorusTwistSign P))) =
      torusWeightSeries (decide (orbitTorusTwistSign P 0 = 1))
          (twistLabel (by simp) (orbitTorusTwistSign P)) *
        mk fun k ↦ if k = 0 then 0 else (SignType.sign (1 - P ^ k).det : ℤ) := by
  simp only [twistLabel_orbitTorusTwistSign, orbitTorusTwistSign_zero, sign_eq_one_iff]
  exact X_mul_derivative_torusWeightSeries_of_det_eq_one hdet hP

end TauCeti
